name intercept-lostlock-1
timeout 280

# THE TACTICALLY DECISIVE CASE: the shooter stops supporting the shot before the round can see for
# itself. This is intercept-aim120.fbm with two changes and nothing else, so the two runs are directly
# comparable:
#
#   1. The viper turns COLD immediately after the launch (its waypoint is 40 km SOUTH, so the pilot rolls
#      into the turn from the first tick and the target walks out of the radar's +-60 deg STT gimbal a
#      dozen seconds later). Losing the lock is therefore a consequence of how the shot was flown — the
#      real reason it happens — and not a switch the mission threw.
#   2. The bandit MANOEUVRES once it is alone: its leg turns north-west, so the constant-velocity
#      extrapolation the missile is left holding walks away from the truth. A target that flew straight
#      would make the inertial phase look better than it is.
#
# The launch is early (t=6 s) so that it happens while the lock still exists — a shot the SMS would
# otherwise refuse, which is itself the interlock working.
#
# WHAT TO READ, in the missile's own telemetry and in events.log:
#   - "missile PHASE ... to=INERTIAL why=uplink lost" and the sim time it happened
#   - msl_tgt_age climbing from then on: the round is flying an estimate that nobody is refreshing
#   - whether the seeker (msl_seeker 1 -> 2) still finds the target inside its +-10 deg field of view
#   - the DETONATION miss distance, or the MISS line with the closest approach it managed
# The honest answer is whatever this prints; both outcomes are informative and neither is tuned for.
# AS IT STANDS after the missile-guidance round it HITS: closest approach 4.12 -> 0.755 m, the bandit is
# combat-ineffective and the run ends exit 1 instead of running both jets out to their waypoints. The
# unsupported round still flies a constant-velocity extrapolation of a manoeuvring target; what changed
# is that its own seeker, once it acquires, is no longer fighting a wound-up acceleration loop.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.70000 8000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 6                    # shoot while the lock is still there, then turn cold
  wp 46.55000 6.72000 8000 400             # 40 km SOUTH: the turn that drops the lock

unit bandit
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.25000 8000 270.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  wp 47.10000 6.90000 8000 400             # north-west: the manoeuvre the stale estimate cannot follow
